 a well-funded independent drawing liberal support", "Alme's large fundraising and institutional backing (NRSC, U.S. Chamber)"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Republican Kurt Alme leading by 20 points or more, all ten expert ratings call the race Safe or Solid R, and prediction markets price Democratic Alani Bankhead's chances near zero. Bankhead's weak fundraising and the independent candidacy of Seth Bodnar, who draws Democratic-leaning support, further fragment the anti-Republican vote.", "watch": "If Bodnar's independent campaign consolidates Democratic-leaning voters behind a single non-Republican alternative, the margin could tighten meaningfully, though a Democratic win would still require a large shift.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Steve Daines (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Montana's open Senate seat leans heavily Republican, and the field is fragmented. Republican Kurt Alme leads polling averages by roughly 20 to 25 points, with Democrat Alani Bankhead running a distant second and independent Seth Bodnar drawing liberal-leaning support, including a Planned Parenthood endorsement that put Bankhead at odds with her own ally. Alme has raised nearly $2 million and enjoys backing from the NRSC and the U.S. Chamber, while outside groups have poured millions into the race on both sides.\n\nAll ten expert ratings place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Bankhead essentially no chance. The main uncertainty is the final margin rather than the winner, with the independent's vote share the biggest variable in how lopsided the result becomes.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -15.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0028, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.004, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0021, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0024, "margin": -